{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Review-plan run 3 PASS (0 blocking); one advisory said the close already reconverges before its gates. Verified: an unforced close runs _refresh_close_material -> ensure_fresh(force=True) -> reconverge first, so on 2e85d8558a4 a completion close with sync.pull on reaches the verifier on the healed store (test passes on main), and review-plan heals with sync.pull on or off (relation snapshot syncs first; passes on main). With REBAR_SYNC_PULL=off the completion close gate DOES refuse with stale-store on main (reproduced), so AC 2 still holds as written. Plan revised: no heal inside store_freshness/claim_gate_check (read-only callers), close heal added to _refresh_close_material regardless of sync.pull, gated claim heals in plan_review_precheck, import heals before its reads, heal uses reconverge's own 2 s lock budget instead of a racy busy-lock probe, heal-failure tests for every new site, docs content stated. AC unchanged; re-running review-plan."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795255120564236001,"uuid":"7e486c80-b103-4e83-8597-aa3a8f84f6bc"}